```

**Caveat on what actually ran:** this was a single-pass review performed entirely in one context — the Agent tool is unavailable here, so there was no multi-agent fan-out and no separate subagent verification pass. I walked the ten angles in sequence myself, re-checked each candidate against the diff, and empirically confirmed findings 1, 2, 3, 9, 10, 13 and 14 by running them (timezone-shifted `adss check` and pytest, DuckDB binder/duplicate-column probes, symlink behaviour, and timings). The rest are reasoned from the code with the failure paths traced by hand.

Lower-severity items that did not make the 15-item cut: `.gitignore:9` documents `uv run adss build --offline`, a flag the new CLI does not have (it is `--live`); `.claude/skills/das/SKILL.md` still says the generated DAS SQL "is committed" while the same commit added `das/sql/` to `.gitignore`; `destinations/app.py:56` and `tests/test_questions.py:66` re-spell `docs/questions` instead of using `Project.questions`, against project.py's own "no path is spelled twice"; `docs/conventions.md` §9 has an orphan table header that renders an empty table above the prose; `platform.py`'s `_open` is a set rather than a counter, so nested opens of the same path would release the `require_detached` guard early (no current call path triggers it); and `read_uss` converts a falsy `attribute:` value to `None` *after* the SUM validation, which would emit a column literally named `"None"`.
